<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.lifehack.doctrine-check — TEMPLATE. Do not load this file as-is: the two __PLACEHOLDERS__
  are filled in by system/launchd/install-doctrine-check.sh, which is the only supported way to
  install it. Rendered copy lands at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.lifehack.doctrine-check.plist.

  WHAT IT IS. The doctrine-sync CHECK side for a machine that does NOT run the pulse. It runs
  `doctrine_sync.py check` every 300 s while the machine is awake (launchd skips sleep and runs
  promptly on wake; it never piles up), writing ONLY this machine's own findings shard
  (state/findings/doctrine-sync-<machine>.local.jsonl). The push side needs nothing: it is the
  PostToolUse hook in .claude/settings.json, which arrives with git pull.

  WHY A LAUNCHAGENT AND NOT A SECOND PULSE. system/tools/install-schedulers.sh chose cron over
  launchd for the pulse, and that decision stands — this is not a reversal of it. The pulse
  itself must run on ONE machine only: two pulses write the same un-namespaced
  state/status/_pulse.json / _system-health.json, and the 2026-08-21 Drive forks
  (health-deadman (1).json, …) are what that looks like. `check` is the ONE job whose only
  output is per-machine by construction, so duplicating it is safe; nothing else in
  pulse-config.md is. Doctrine, in one line: PULSE ON THE MACHINE THAT RUNS THE PULSE; A
  CHECK-ONLY LAUNCHAGENT ON ANY OTHER. The installer refuses on a machine whose crontab already
  carries pulse.sh, so the rule is enforced, not merely written down.

  FIRST PROVEN 2026-08-22 on a second Mac (hand-built there; this template is the
  repeatable form of it): kick-start exit 0, two OK rows; first unattended tick 14:21, exit 0.

  IF THE LOG SHOWS "Operation not permitted" on the notes path: that is macOS TCC / Full Disk
  Access refusing /usr/bin/python3 a cloud-synced folder (the A38 failure install-schedulers.sh
  records). It did NOT occur on the first machine; if it occurs on yours, grant Full Disk Access
  to the python3 binary in System Settings → Privacy & Security. INFERRED remedy, not yet needed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.lifehack.doctrine-check</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>__REPO__/system/tools/doctrine_sync.py</string>
    <string>check</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__REPO__</string>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>300</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.local/state/lifehack/doctrine-check.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.local/state/lifehack/doctrine-check.log</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
